From 94c132b633628129cabb0cc5afdba33e3377496f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:34:13 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Input: the keypad's numbers with Num Lock off bind as keys of
 their own

Keys are bound by their place on the keyboard (SDL's scancodes), and
SDL reports a keypad number key at the same place with Num Lock on or
off, so Keypad 8 was Keypad 8 either way. A keyboard player moved with
the keypad's 8 4 5 6 on a PSP emulator and pressed Num Lock to turn the
same keys into the camera, which Windows' own keys allowed there: with
Num Lock off the keypad sends the keys printed under its numbers.

Now those are keys of their own, named after the keys printed under the
numbers: Keypad Up (8), Keypad Clear (5), Keypad Home (7) and so on, at
positions SDL leaves unused (501-511). A keypad key bound both ways
presses its number's control with Num Lock on and the other with it
off; bound only one way, it presses that control whatever Num Lock
says, so keypads bound before, or bound with Num Lock off and played
with it on, play as they did. They are not the arrow keys.

- input/bindings: the names, num_lock_off_position(), keypad_number_of(),
  typed_position() and key_held().
- gpu/vulkan_renderer: the game's key read asks SDL's Num Lock through
  key_held(); <prefix>_TRACE_PAD logs Num Lock as it changes.
- ui/layer: the Controls page binds a keypad key pressed with Num Lock
  off as its Num Lock off key.
- <prefix>_NO_NUM_LOCK_KEYS=1 reads and binds the numbers whatever Num
  Lock says (the old behaviour).
- ui/input_script: `numlock on|off` sets SDL's Num Lock, and the key
  events it sends carry SDL's modifiers.
- tests: the Num Lock cases; the settings tests' target gets
  host/input/players.cpp, without which it did not link.
- PROFILE_GUIDE: the keypad's keys with Num Lock off.

Tested on Windows (the game built with llvm-mingw clang, the framework
tests with MSVC) with Dissidia 012 and the keyboard only, scripted: with Move on Keypad 8 4 5
6 and the D-pad also on Keypad Up, Clear, Left and Right, Num Lock on
moved the stick and Num Lock off pressed the D-pad, the arrow keys
pressed the D-pad either way and unbound keypad keys nothing; with
nothing scripted the game read Num Lock on as Windows had it; the
Controls page with Num Lock off bound Keypad 8 as Keypad Up and Keypad
5 as Keypad Clear and saved them. The framework tests pass but the ad
hoc ones, not run. Not tested: the real Num Lock key pressed while the
game runs, a battle, Linux, the Steam Deck, Android, another game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
